(D3 — Discrepancy 3 repro: LANGUAGE.md:4141-4144 says the list-variable
 form builds argv "from the list's current length and contents, sized and
 bounds-checked from that single length read so the argv array cannot be
 overrun regardless of the list's contents". The bounds claim holds — this
 does not crash. But a single non-text element makes the exec fail
 outright, which the manual never says, and "regardless of the list's
 contents" reads like a promise that it would not.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/D3.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   one number in the list was enough to fail the exec
)
a list called 'the arguments' is [42].
Execute "/bin/echo" with arguments 'the arguments'.
On error print "one number in the list was enough to fail the exec".
